            <ArticleTitle>Report on the first PVL-positive community acquired MRSA strain in Latvia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2807/esm.09.11.00485-en</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Infections by community-acquired methicillin resistant Staphylococcus aureus (CA-MRSA) have been reported worldwide. Here we present characterisation of the first CA-MRSA isolated in Latvia. A PVL-positive ST30-MRSA-IV strain was isolated from a nasal swab and the central venous catheter of a patient with fever and multiple organ failure. The PFGE pattern of this strain was identical to pattern SE00-3 of MRSA isolated in Sweden from 29 patients during 2000-2003. This strain is related to the South Pacific area, and its appearance in Sweden and Latvia demonstrates its global spread.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
